---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Nimbo - Support"
  description="Get help with Nimbo - Mood Journal, the iOS app: checking in from the widget and the daily nudge, importing from Mood Easy, exporting, and Apple Health."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/nimbo/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Nimbo?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Nimbo%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What do the five weathers mean?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Sunny is a great day. Mild is good and steady. Clear is just a normal day: calm, nothing in the air. Drizzly is a bit low. Stormy is rough, or on edge. Pick the one that fits; there are no scores.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I check in without opening the app?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Add the Check in widget to your Home Screen (touch and hold the Home Screen, tap Edit, then Add Widget, and choose Nimbo), then tap a weather in it. You can also long-press the daily nudge and pick a weather, use the Nimbo button in Control Center or the Action button, or say &ldquo;Check in with Nimbo&rdquo; to Siri.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I set up the daily nudge?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Tap the settings button on Today, then under Daily nudge turn on Nimbo floats by and choose a time. Turn on Weekends too if you&rsquo;d like it every day. The nudge is skipped on days you&rsquo;ve already checked in, and your Apple Watch gets it too.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I change or fill in a past day?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. In Sky, tap any day to see it, change it, or fill in one you missed.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I move my history over from Mood Easy?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">In Mood Easy, go to Settings &rarr; Data &rarr; Export check-ins and save the file. Then in Nimbo, open Settings and tap Import from Mood Easy under Your data, and choose that file. Great to Awful become Sunny to Stormy.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I export my check-ins?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">In Settings, under Your data, tap Export every check-in for a CSV with the date, weather, tags and note of every day. Tap Summary for your therapist for the last 30 days as a calm one-page PDF.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How does Apple Health work?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">In Settings, turn on Save to Apple Health (iOS 18 and later). Nimbo then saves each day&rsquo;s weather as State of Mind. That&rsquo;s all it shares: notes and tags never leave Nimbo, and nothing is read from Health. If Nimbo isn&rsquo;t allowed to save, turn it on in the Health app under Sharing &rarr; Apps &rarr; Nimbo.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can Nimbo move less?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Nimbo follows Reduce Motion: turn it on in the iPhone Settings app under Accessibility &rarr; Motion, and Nimbo and his weather hold still.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I see the first-launch walkthrough again?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. In Settings, tap Meet Nimbo again.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is Nimbo a replacement for therapy?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">No. Nimbo is a journal, not medical care. If you&rsquo;re struggling, please talk to someone you trust or a professional. In the US, you can call or text <a href="tel:988" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">988</a> any time.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
